wer-defense-game",[177],[491,492],{"_51":95,"_26":96},{"_51":420,"_26":421},[494],{"_51":495,"_26":496,"_194":497},"Read the author’s agent attribution","https://github.com/Aleksandr-Litvinenko/Codex.-Crown-Defender-TD-3D-browser-tower-defense-game/blob/main/COMPARISON.md","Author-published Russian comparison explicitly states that Codex built this version from the same requirements as the Claude Code project; no raw session is published.",[499],{"_51":500,"_26":488,"_194":501},"Open the complete Codex game project","Includes game.js, interface, bundled Three.js, runtime textures, requirements and optional WebSocket relay. No build or dependency installation for solo play. MIT code; see ASSET_CREDITS.md.","download",[504],{"_51":505,"_26":506,"_194":507},"Download and run Crown Defender","https://github.com/Aleksandr-Litvinenko/Codex.-Crown-Defender-TD-3D-browser-tower-defense-game/archive/refs/heads/main.zip","Static browser game. Run python3 -m http.server 8010 and open localhost:8010/index.html; choose Играть (Play). Russian interface. WASD/arrows move; semicolon attacks. Mobile joystick/buttons included. Optional two-player mode requires node server/multiplayer-server.mjs.","Source download",[510],{"_51":511,"_26":496,"_194":-7},"Read the same-brief agent comparison",[513,514,515,516],"Serve the project locally and enter TD Defense.","Read the original requirements and same-brief comparison.","Inspect hero movement, wave progression and upgrade logic.","Change one upgrade and test losing, retrying and saved progress.","Aleksandr-Litvinenko attributes this build to Codex and publishes a comparison with a Claude Code version made from the same brief. The author states that the comparison concerns the agents’ original implementation choices, with assets and runtime code included here.","AI-generated (creator attribution)","ai-generated",[513,514,515,516],{"_51":511,"_26":496,"_18":318},{"_51":505,"_26":506,"_18":502,"_194":507},{"_51":500,"_26":488,"_247":248,"_194